[[Image:Walnut03.jpg|thumb|right|The expression refers to the tidy, compact package.]]
==English==

===Etymology===
A calque of {{etyl|la|-}} {{term|in nuce|lang=la}}.

===Adverb===
{{head|en|adverb|head=[[in]] [[a]] [[nutshell]]}}

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} In summary; [[briefly]] or [[simply]].
#: ''He had a lot to say, but his answer, '''in a nutshell''', was no.''
#*'''1899''', Joseph Conrad, ''[[s:Heart of Darkness|Heart of Darkness]]'', [[s:Heart of Darkness/Section I|section 1]]
#*:The yarns of seamen have a direct simplicity, the whole meaning of which lies '''within the shell of a cracked nut'''. 
